Verdict
-------
PASS. Both blocks polled the shared executor. Retaining a terminal Waker kept
one slot out of the free pool, giving exactly 255 High admissions plus one
NoFreeSlots rejection. Dropping it released the reclaim, reused the same slot
at generation 1 -> 2, and left the old TaskKey Stale. All 256 TwoPoll tasks
polled exactly twice and completed once.

Phase3 used real typed APIs: the Low donor uniquely moved its executor-issued
token through release/acquire storage; the High target entered the code path
that necessarily returns Pending and issued a real self-wake before the READY
publication. Shutdown then produced Cancelled, replay produced AlreadyJoined,
pending reclaims fell 2 -> 1 -> 0 after handle/token release, all seven runners
exited, and final spawned/completed were 515 with active/context refs/pending
reclaims all zero and can_teardown true. The event is published inside poll
before Poll::Pending returns, so this evidence does not claim that shutdown is
externally ordered after the poll call has returned.
